<title>JAPAN: Japan trade surplus falls 29.6 pct in 96/97.</title>
<headline>Japan trade surplus falls 29.6 pct in 96/97.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's customs-cleared trade surplus for fiscal 1996/97 year fell 29.6 percent from a year earlier to 6.42 trillion yen, the Finance Ministry said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>    (Unadjusted data, in million yen) 1996/97   1995/96     PCT CHG</p>
<p>  Overall balance		+6,421,250    +9,116,476   -29.6</p>
<p>    Exports			46,050,054    42,069,432    +9.5</p>
<p>    Imports			39,628,804    32,952,956   +20.3</p>
<p> (Country breakdown)	 1996/97	  PCT CHG</p>
<p>  With U.S.		   +3,762,697	  -2.2</p>
<p>    Exports		   12,673,716	 +11.6</p>
<p>    Imports		    8,911,019	 +18.7</p>
<p>  With EU		     +1,433,550	 -26.6</p>
<p>    Exports		    6,982,690	  +4.1</p>
<p>    Imports		    5,549,140	 +16.8</p>
<p>  With Asia		   +5,408,982	 -15.7</p>
<p>    Exports		   19,880,375	  +7.9</p>
<p>    Imports		   14,471,393	 +20.5</p>
<p>  With China		  -2,252,540	 +54.9</p>
<p>    Exports		    2,405,599	 +12.9</p>
<p>    Imports		    4,658,139	 +29.9</p>
<p>  With Asian NIEs	   +6,804,092	  +5.1</p>
<p>    Exports		   11,235,786	  +6.3</p>
<p>    Imports		    4,431,694	  +8.3</p>
</text>
